# Day 3 - Project Structure & Shared Module

## Objective
Refactor the project into a scalable Maven multi-module structure and introduce a reusable shared module.

## Completed
- Refactored backend folder to `platform-services`
- Created Maven multi-module architecture
- Added parent `platform-services/pom.xml`
- Created `platform-common` reusable JAR module
- Connected `customer-service` with `platform-common`
- Added generic `ApiResponse<T>`
- Added `ApplicationConstants`
- Updated Customer Service health API to use shared components
- Kept service-specific configuration in `application.properties`

## Project Structure

platform-services/
├── pom.xml
├── platform-common/
└── customer-service/

## Architecture Decision
`platform-common` contains reusable technical components shared across services. It is a library module, not an independently running Spring Boot microservice.

Each business microservice remains independently runnable and deployable.

